[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi all<br>\nFor the past few days, I have been working on a formalisation of Gronwall's inequality in differential form, with variable constants (this is listed as a TODO in Gronwall.lean).<br>\n I have largely followed the proof given on Wikipedia, as I found it the easiest to follow. Since I have only been working with Lean for a few weeks, my code seems rather cumbersome compared with other code I have seen.<br>\n The formalisation comprises three theorems.</p>\n<p>I struggled with the main theorem, so I asked an LLM for help and had it explain its suggestions to me. This seemed to me rather like using a spell-checker. However, I want to make sure that I am not wasting anyone's time or being misleading. I would therefore appreciate feedback on whether this would count as LLM-assisted rather than LLM-generated code, and whether it would be appropriate to submit the formalisation as a contribution to Mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 632176488,
        "sender_full_name": "Uwe Brauer",
        "timestamp": 1792135089
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>not an offial comment about currently applied guidelines, but the best way to ensure you're not \"wasting anybody's time\" is by iterating over your code several times and ensure you are really happy with it. It's not only about getting X into the library, but also about thinking about the relevant API surrounding that topic. Was it simple to proof X? Was something on the way missing which would have made the experience much smoother? Is X useful to adding more maths in the future? By the sounds of it you are already doing that to some extend :)</p>\n<p>If a PR is of this quality (and is presented in parsable junks/dependent PRs), I personally think it's mostly irrelevant if you used an LLM to get there. The problem we currently have is that many people stop at \"LLM produced some proof of X\" and never look at the library around X.</p>",
        "id": 632217509,
        "sender_full_name": "Jon Eugster",
        "timestamp": 1792145626
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Even though mathlib maintainers have various opinions about AI and disagree about the exact phrasing/implementation of the following rule, we do not encourage low-quality AI-assisted PRs to mathlib by new contributors.<br>\nI would like to say that it is quite important to \"play\" with Lean for a certain time (learning how to write Lean code using appropriate tactics, learning by reading proofs by others, etc). Even if they are related, formalising a lemma, and contributing its proof to mathlib are two different tasks, and were already very different before the AI thing. If you want to learn the Lean language for proving theorems, you are very much welcome to ask questions/feedback in channels like \"new members\" or \"Is there code for X?\". When you feel more confident about the code you produce, you may consider making PRs to mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 632224235,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1792147041
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"385895\">Jon Eugster</span> <a href=\"#narrow/near/632217509\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>not an offial comment about currently applied guidelines, but the best way to ensure you're not \"wasting anybody's time\" is by iterating over your code several times and ensure you are really happy with it. It's not only about getting X into the library, but also about thinking about the relevant API surrounding that topic. Was it simple to proof X? Was something on the way missing which would have made the experience much smoother? Is X useful to adding more maths in the future? By the sounds of it you are already doing that to some extend <span aria-label=\"slight smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f642\" role=\"img\" title=\"slight smile\">:slight_smile:</span></p>\n<p>If a PR is of this quality (and is presented in parsable junks/dependent PRs), I personally think it's mostly irrelevant if you used an LLM to get there. The problem we currently have is that many people stop at \"LLM produced some proof of X\" and never look at the library around X.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>thanks, here is a very simple example</p>\n<p>For the version of Gronwall's lemma I want to formalize I need </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- If `φ` is continuous on `[a, b]` and `a ≤ b`, then its primitive `t ↦ ∫ s in a..t, φ s`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">is continuous on `[a, b]`. -/</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So I came up with this</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuousOn_primitive_of_continuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hφ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Icc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Icc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Icc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uIcc_of_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntegrableOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">volume</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hφ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">integrableOn_compact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isCompact_Icc</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuousOn_primitive_interval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hint</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>When I asked the LLM about it he proposed first</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuousOn_primitive_of_continuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hφ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Icc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Icc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntegrableOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">volume</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc_of_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hφ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">integrableOn_compact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isCompact_Icc</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuousOn_primitive_interval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hint</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rwa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc_of_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>When I told him I don't know <code>rwa</code> and I rather would avoid it  he proposed this,</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuousOn_primitive_of_continuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hφ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Icc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Icc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntegrableOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">volume</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc_of_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hφ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">integrableOn_compact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isCompact_Icc</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">continuousOn_primitive_interval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hint</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc_of_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But I sticked to my version</p>",
